WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.580
In 1614, Japan's rulers
banned Christianity.

2
00:00:04.630 --> 00:00:07.110
Some Japanese Christians went into hiding,

3
00:00:07.160 --> 00:00:11.100
and kept their faith in
secret for over 200 years.

4
00:00:11.150 --> 00:00:15.930
Across the Pacific, in Mexico,
Catholics honor the Virgin of Guadalupe,

5
00:00:15.980 --> 00:00:20.430
who they believe appeared on
a hill called Tepeyac in 1531.

6
00:00:20.480 --> 00:00:24.720
So when faiths met
across oceans after 1492,

7
00:00:24.770 --> 00:00:29.490
why did some spread, some get
banned, and some grow new forms?

8
00:00:29.540 --> 00:00:33.390
In this mission, you'll follow
missionaries from Europe to the Americas,

9
00:00:33.440 --> 00:00:35.150
Africa and Asia.

10
00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:40.820
Then you'll weigh up a big claim: that
religions spread mainly through force.

11
00:00:40.870 --> 00:00:44.000
Your mission: find out
why some faiths spread,

12
00:00:44.050 --> 00:00:47.070
some were banned, and some grew new forms.
